# local-mariadb

Local MariaDB instance for development. Runs as a Docker container with persistent volume to keep the databases.

## Requirements

- [Docker](https://docs.docker.com/get-docker/)
- [Docker Compose](https://docs.docker.com/compose/install/)

## Installation

```bash
cp .env.example .env
# Adjust the password and/or the portnumber in the .env
```

## Usage

```bash
# Start up.
docker compose up -d

# Stopping (databases are persistent)
docker compose stop

# Stopping and container removal (data persistent in the volume)
docker compose down

# Checking logs
docker compose logs -f

# Full container removal including data
docker compose down -v
```

## Connecting

| Setting  | Value                        |
|----------|------------------------------|
| Host     | `127.0.0.1`                  |
| Poort    | See `MARIADB_PORT` in `.env` |
| User     | `root`                       |
| Password | See `.env`                   |

## Create a project specific database and user.

Connect as root and perform the following query::

```sql
CREATE DATABASE project_name CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
CREATE USER 'project_user'@'%' IDENTIFIED BY 'project_user_password';
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON project_name.* TO 'project_user'@'%';
FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
```

Through the CLI from the container:

```bash
docker exec -it local-mariadb mariadb -u root -p
```
